WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.408
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:02.117 --> 00:00:05.658
Well, now that you've moved in, I see
you're making yourself right at home.

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:07.242
You're not, like, into him, are you?

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.575
You told Summer you weren't coming.
Now you're here with him?

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:11.533
- Ryan and I aren't here together.
- We're done.

00:00:11.742 --> 00:00:14.575
I can't say no to my family.
I'll pay everything back.

00:00:14.783 --> 00:00:18.283
- Put your feelings for him aside.
- He's one of my oldest friends.

00:00:18.492 --> 00:00:21.867
Are you telling me you lost everything?
That is my money! My kids' tuition!

00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:24.783
- I'm sorry.
- Son of a bitch! You're a thief!

00:00:24.992 --> 00:00:27.867
- I'm sorry.
- I just need to be alone right now.

00:01:01.492 --> 00:01:03.533
So, what are we doing
in front of this tank?

00:01:03.742 --> 00:01:06.117
Ryan, we're like two samurai, really.

00:01:06.325 --> 00:01:10.450
And we need to have respect
for each other before meeting in battle.

00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:14.200
And eating lobster is a battle,
as you will soon learn.

00:01:14.408 --> 00:01:15.992
Is that a new shirt?

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.575
Yeah. Your mom bought me some new
clothes, which she didn't have to do.

00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:22.450
Right. You can get a lot of mileage
out of a tank top.

00:01:22.658 --> 00:01:25.492
Hey, do you think I could pull off
the wife-beater?

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.742
You know, switch up my look?

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.950
Got you. You got your style, I got mine.

00:01:31.158 --> 00:01:33.117
- Yeah.
- You're dead.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:40.325
That was amazing.
A lot of work, but amazing.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.283
What's going on with you and Marissa?
Did you talk to her?

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.325
I don't think she wants to talk.

00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:49.117
- Everything with her and her dad...
- Do you know what your problem is?

00:01:49.325 --> 00:01:52.283
And I speak from experience,
with great authority here.

00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:55.367
Is that you really need
to be aggressive, okay?

00:01:55.575 --> 00:01:59.617
Her and Luke broke up. You need to go
after her, tell her how you feel. It's easy.

00:01:59.825 --> 00:02:02.908
What do we do? Where do we go?
I have no car, no money.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:08.575
I got it. I picked up extra sailing lessons
this week. Feeling a little bit flush.

00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:10.533
Not you too. I can't keep doing this.

00:02:10.742 --> 00:02:14.033
Your parents pay for everything.
I can't keep taking their money.

00:02:14.242 --> 00:02:16.575
- They're parents. They work for us.
- They're your parents.

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:19.450
They're your guardians.
It's the same principle.

00:02:19.658 --> 00:02:22.617
- What are you gonna do for cash, then?
- You're out of here!

00:02:22.825 --> 00:02:25.158
You can't fire me. I quit!

00:02:32.825 --> 00:02:35.658
Fine. But you're hooking me up
with free lobster.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.367
This actually works out good for me,
you starting the new job.

00:03:10.575 --> 00:03:14.450
I'll have time to do that stuff I haven't
been able to do since you moved here...

00:03:14.658 --> 00:03:16.533
...like I'm gonna get to start my novel.

00:03:16.742 --> 00:03:18.033
I'll be back by 6.

00:03:18.242 --> 00:03:19.950
Yeah. I know. It's 9 now.

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:23.117
Which means I'm gonna have
nine hours of "me" time.

00:03:23.325 --> 00:03:25.117
Know what I'm saying? For me, Ryan.

00:03:25.325 --> 00:03:28.242
I'm gonna do stuff like learn Chinese,
study my Talmud.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:29.950
You know, sink my teeth into it.

00:03:30.158 --> 00:03:31.867
You gonna be okay?

00:03:32.075 --> 00:03:33.408
Yes. Before you moved here...

00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:36.783
...all I did was hang out by myself,
so it's really a return to form.

00:03:36.992 --> 00:03:38.450
Should we not go?

00:03:38.658 --> 00:03:41.700
Maybe we could tell Julie
we're not going and go anyway.

00:03:41.908 --> 00:03:45.408
You guys, that's too mean.
We can't do that. Can we, Kirsten?

00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:49.117
Absolutely not. We've had this retreat
on the books now for months.

00:03:49.325 --> 00:03:50.950
And Julie's looking forward to it.

00:03:51.158 --> 00:03:54.283
Yeah, and some of us
were looking forward to retiring early...

00:03:54.492 --> 00:03:56.492
...before her husband stole our money.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.742
Dad. What are you doing, man?

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.200
I'm waiting for them to disperse.

00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:04.617
I left my briefcase in there.
I need to get to work.

00:04:04.825 --> 00:04:08.283
- Well, go get it.
- And talk to those women? I can't.

00:04:08.492 --> 00:04:10.450
He didn't steal. It wasn't like...

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.075
She's our friend.

00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:16.908
I can't believe you're defending them.
Jimmy Cooper's a thief and a felon.

00:04:17.408 --> 00:04:18.617
Those women are obsessed.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:21.408
You kidding?
A scandal this big in a town this small...

00:04:21.617 --> 00:04:23.575
...they'll be dining out
on this for months.

00:04:23.783 --> 00:04:27.117
What are their kids gonna do?
I mean, with their father in prison?

00:04:27.325 --> 00:04:29.742
- You think he's going to jail?
- I heard 10 to 20.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.742
- Is it true he's going to jail?
- He stole a lot of money...

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.158
...from powerful people.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.783
What's Marissa gonna do
without her dad?

00:04:36.992 --> 00:04:39.200
No one knows if she'll even wanna go.

00:04:39.408 --> 00:04:43.367
I don't want to go, I have to go.
The trip's already been paid for.

00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:48.325
Besides, if I don't show up, they'll spend
the entire weekend gossiping about me.

00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:50.033
You're being a little paranoid.

00:04:50.242 --> 00:04:53.617
No, I'm not. I'm sure they think
I've masterminded this whole debacle.

00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:55.867
Honey, they're your friends.

00:04:56.075 --> 00:04:59.158
Please. They're the gatekeepers
of this entire community...

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:02.533
...a community your daughters and I
would like to remain a part of.

00:05:02.742 --> 00:05:06.700
This is my chance to go before the firing
squad and plead for a stay of execution.

00:05:06.908 --> 00:05:10.325
I was hoping to be able to talk
this weekend.

00:05:10.533 --> 00:05:13.200
This is your mess, Jimmy.
You clean it up.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:17.575
And when I get back, we'll figure out
what the hell we're gonna tell our girls.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.242
I'm totally crispy.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:29.200
Let's go do something.
Shopping, get exfoliated, anything.

00:05:29.408 --> 00:05:32.825
And pay for it how? I mean, my dad's
credit cards got shut off yesterday.

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:35.283
What about Luke?
I mean, he can pay for you.

00:05:35.867 --> 00:05:38.617
- He is your boyfriend, right?
- I don't know.

00:05:40.325 --> 00:05:42.075
We left things kind of up in the air.

00:05:42.283 --> 00:05:47.367
- You haven't talked since cotillion?
- I haven't talked to anyone, except you.

00:05:48.533 --> 00:05:51.117
Okay, this is so not the way
to handle this.

00:05:51.325 --> 00:05:54.325
You're gonna become depressed.
Then you'll need medication...

00:05:54.533 --> 00:05:57.492
...and then you're gonna stop
feeling like anything.

00:05:57.992 --> 00:06:00.117
According to my stepmom.

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:05.950
Let me buy you lunch. My dad gave me
his credit card in case of emergencies.

00:06:06.158 --> 00:06:09.533
- And, well, this is an emergency.
- Okay.

00:06:09.742 --> 00:06:12.200
All right, man, I'm gonna give you
the rundown.

00:06:14.117 --> 00:06:15.450
This...

00:06:15.825 --> 00:06:17.117
...is garbage.

00:06:17.325 --> 00:06:19.492
It belongs in the garbage.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.408
This belongs over here.

00:06:23.242 --> 00:06:25.700
And now for the advanced class.

00:06:25.908 --> 00:06:30.033
Hello, Mrs. Palmer. How are you today?
Would you like another glass of merlot?

00:06:30.242 --> 00:06:31.908
Coming right up.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.908
Drunk.

00:06:35.117 --> 00:06:37.367
- Been working here long?
- Oh, man, too long.

00:06:37.575 --> 00:06:41.492
Everybody who comes in is a freak show.
They like $30 entrees on plastic plates...

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:46.242
...$60 bottles of wine in plastic cups,
and service with a big smile.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:49.325
Welcome to Newport,
where things only appear to be casual.

00:06:50.575 --> 00:06:53.617
Of course,
living here does have its upside.

00:06:53.825 --> 00:06:55.825
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:06:57.492 --> 00:06:59.075
First day on the job.

00:06:59.825 --> 00:07:03.117
Well, the food here is really good.

00:07:03.575 --> 00:07:05.200
Yeah.

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:08.617
- How's your dad?
- He's okay.

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:12.408
- How are you?
- Coop! Starving.

00:07:13.783 --> 00:07:15.908
- I should get back to work.
- Right.

00:07:16.117 --> 00:07:18.783
You wanna hang out sometime?
Go out?

00:07:19.908 --> 00:07:22.742
- Like on a date?
- Not a date, just...

00:07:24.283 --> 00:07:26.117
- I can't right now.
- No, of course.

00:07:26.742 --> 00:07:28.825
- Right.
- But thanks.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:32.617
See you.

00:07:38.325 --> 00:07:40.367
Hey, Jimmy.

00:07:44.408 --> 00:07:47.575
- How's it going?
- Never better.

00:07:47.783 --> 00:07:51.408
Listen, I was thinking, how would you
like some free legal advice?

00:07:52.033 --> 00:07:55.617
You wanna be my lawyer? How long
do you wanna send me away for?

00:07:55.825 --> 00:07:58.533
- I got way too big an ego for that.
- Well, that's true.

00:07:58.742 --> 00:08:02.367
I wouldn't be representing you. I have
a friend who's a securities attorney.

00:08:02.575 --> 00:08:04.492
But I could help you
put together a case.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.117
Why? You don't even like me.

00:08:07.367 --> 00:08:09.533
Well, I'm a public defender.

00:08:09.742 --> 00:08:12.408
I represent a lot of people I don't like.

00:08:18.325 --> 00:08:20.658
I wish somebody had told me
he worked here now.

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:22.075
- Why?
- No reason.

00:08:23.117 --> 00:08:25.783
Oh, what do you know? Luke.

00:08:27.117 --> 00:08:29.033
- What a coincidence.
- You invited him?

00:08:29.242 --> 00:08:31.992
- Gotta pee. See you.
- Wait, Summer.

00:08:34.617 --> 00:08:36.575
Hey, man.

00:08:40.867 --> 00:08:42.908
- Hey, babe.
- Hey.

00:08:45.283 --> 00:08:48.408
I hate that kid, man.
I seriously hate that kid.

00:08:48.617 --> 00:08:50.242
He walks in like he owns the place.

00:08:51.117 --> 00:08:54.742
Let me tell you, that Abercrombie &amp; Fitch
water-polo-playing bitch...

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:57.033
...wouldn't last two minutes in Corona.

00:08:57.242 --> 00:08:59.075
- You're from Corona?
- Yeah, man.

00:08:59.283 --> 00:09:01.742
- Chino.
- Chino?

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.242
It's a long way from home.
That place is no joke.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.117
I'm sorry I haven't called you back.

00:09:06.325 --> 00:09:09.950
No worries.
We don't have to talk about it.

00:09:10.158 --> 00:09:11.867
- Maybe we should talk about it.
- Why?

00:09:12.075 --> 00:09:15.992
Talking about stuff is just gonna get us
all bummed out. Let's just do something.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.117
- Newport kids must make you sick too.
- Sounds like you're a fan.

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:22.617
You know, I like the surf,
I like the tips, love the girls.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.325
It's not all like this.
There's some real people around here.

00:09:26.533 --> 00:09:27.908
- Oh, yeah?
- I tell you what.

00:09:28.117 --> 00:09:30.992
After work, I'll show you
what I'm talking about. Cool?

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.658
Cool.

00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:37.825
Holly's beach house. Party.

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:39.783
- I don't really want to.
- Why not?

00:09:39.992 --> 00:09:44.617
It's weird. I mean, her dad beat up
my dad at my debutante ball.

00:09:44.825 --> 00:09:48.617
You can't blame Holly for that.
I mean, your dad stole all their mon...

00:09:50.158 --> 00:09:51.742
Nice.

00:10:12.367 --> 00:10:15.325
Normally we don't tip out to trainees,
but you did good, man.

00:10:15.533 --> 00:10:17.825
- Thanks.
- All right, now you can buy me a beer.

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:20.908
- I'm gonna grab my sweatshirt.
- All right.

00:10:29.658 --> 00:10:31.283
- Hey.
- What's up?

00:10:31.492 --> 00:10:35.367
Craziest thing. I was in the neighborhood,
checked my watch, it's 6:00...

00:10:35.575 --> 00:10:38.575
...I figured maybe we'd celebrate
your first day on the job.

00:10:38.783 --> 00:10:40.200
- Yeah.
- Yo, kid. You ready?

00:10:40.408 --> 00:10:44.408
Yeah. I made other plans. This is Donnie.
He grew up in a town next to me.

00:10:44.617 --> 00:10:46.283
- Donnie, Seth.
- What's up, man?

00:10:46.492 --> 00:10:50.158
Hey, what's up? You guys must
have a lot of catching up to do.

00:10:50.367 --> 00:10:55.742
Got some girls we gotta catch up with.
The blond's a dancer.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.908
Yes. The ladies. I feel you.

00:11:00.117 --> 00:11:02.283
Well, do you wanna...?
Donnie, is it cool...?

00:11:02.492 --> 00:11:05.867
No, no, no. Please, no.
You guys go. I have to...

00:11:06.075 --> 00:11:09.242
I was gonna do stuff.
Donnie, it was really good to meet you.

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.575
- All right, man. Let's go.
- See you.

00:11:11.783 --> 00:11:15.158
So then I'll see you at home tomorrow.

00:11:15.367 --> 00:11:17.700
Or tonight. I don't know. Just go.

00:11:17.908 --> 00:11:20.617
- You sure you don't want to...?
- No, no. Just...

00:11:20.825 --> 00:11:22.992
- All right.
- Okay.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.533
Have fun.

00:11:58.158 --> 00:11:59.742
What are you reading?

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.117
The new Legion came out Wednesday.

00:12:02.742 --> 00:12:04.908
- It's part two of five.
- I liked part one.

00:12:05.117 --> 00:12:07.408
Yeah, I'll let you borrow it
when I'm done.

00:12:08.783 --> 00:12:10.492
Thanks.

00:12:11.492 --> 00:12:12.658
How was last night?

00:12:12.867 --> 00:12:14.283
- Fun.
- Cool.

00:12:15.492 --> 00:12:19.533
That's cool that, you know, you met
someone that's where you're from.

00:12:19.742 --> 00:12:22.450
You know, it's just cool.

00:12:34.117 --> 00:12:36.908
I mean, I know he's not
the most sensitive guy in the world.

00:12:37.117 --> 00:12:39.825
No one wants to see you
with Luke more than me.

00:12:40.033 --> 00:12:42.367
But what you're going through
right now is gnarly.

00:12:42.575 --> 00:12:45.242
Luke's a boy. Maybe he can't handle it.

00:12:45.783 --> 00:12:47.408
Is it bad to burn on top of a peel?

00:12:49.533 --> 00:12:51.908
Yeah. Put 30 on.

00:12:52.117 --> 00:12:53.950
Coop, your life will stabilize.

00:12:54.158 --> 00:12:57.367
Your parents will work it out.
Your mom will go away this weekend...

00:12:57.575 --> 00:12:59.742
...they'll miss each other
and have makeup sex.

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:02.950
- Summer. God.
- It's true.

00:13:04.783 --> 00:13:06.283
Marissa.

00:13:06.783 --> 00:13:08.242
Hi.

00:13:10.742 --> 00:13:14.242
- I'm just heading to the office.
- Yeah, me too.

00:13:15.742 --> 00:13:18.200
- You know what...?
- I was thinking...

00:13:19.033 --> 00:13:21.408
When I asked you to hang out,
I was asking you out.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.450
- I know.
- I wanted to clear that up...

00:13:23.658 --> 00:13:25.617
...because I'm gonna ask you out again.

00:13:25.825 --> 00:13:27.867
Do you wanna do something tonight?

00:13:28.075 --> 00:13:30.075
I have to babysit for Kaitlin.

00:13:30.283 --> 00:13:33.658
But I will be cooking.
Macaroni and cheese. It's my specialty.

00:13:33.867 --> 00:13:35.950
So that's a yes.

00:13:36.158 --> 00:13:37.617
All right.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:43.367
Won't these costs
be covered by Chapter 11?

00:13:43.575 --> 00:13:46.242
Well, filing for bankruptcy
won't make this go away.

00:13:46.408 --> 00:13:49.325
The U.S. Attorney's Office
is involved in this now.

00:13:49.533 --> 00:13:52.033
They'll push for fraud,
unauthorized transactions.

00:13:52.242 --> 00:13:55.117
Okay, so they fine me,
I go back to work, I make it all back.

00:13:55.325 --> 00:13:59.325
Four million dollars? Unless you plan on
going to the track and getting lucky...

00:13:59.533 --> 00:14:01.908
Look, if you don't wanna do this...

00:14:02.117 --> 00:14:04.617
You're gonna lose your Series 7 license.

00:14:04.825 --> 00:14:07.700
It's important that you understand
the predicament you're in.

00:14:07.908 --> 00:14:09.533
Look...

00:14:09.742 --> 00:14:13.283
...I get it from my wife every day,
my daughters won't talk to me...

00:14:13.492 --> 00:14:18.200
...I got beat up in front of everyone
at the most elegant event of the year.

00:14:18.408 --> 00:14:20.908
I get it. Okay, man?
I definitely understand.

00:14:22.283 --> 00:14:24.617
Well, look. You know, we're both tired.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:28.408
Maybe we should take a break,
go out.

00:14:28.617 --> 00:14:30.325
What do you wanna do?

00:14:30.533 --> 00:14:33.700
Well, our wives are away
for the weekend. We could...

00:14:34.908 --> 00:14:37.450
Well, what did we do
before we got married?

00:14:37.658 --> 00:14:39.533
Put that thing away, Kirsten.

00:14:39.742 --> 00:14:41.158
I'm sorry.

00:14:41.367 --> 00:14:45.533
We put a bid in on a new development,
and the counteroffer's outrageous.

00:14:45.742 --> 00:14:49.533
We're here to relax.
Just because you have a job...

00:14:49.742 --> 00:14:52.158
She's lucky she has a career.

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:55.117
I mean, it's not luck.
You're a very hard worker.

00:14:56.658 --> 00:15:00.200
God knows I could use
my own income right about now.

00:15:00.742 --> 00:15:04.367
Let's say it. I better enjoy the weekend
because I won't be back for a while.

00:15:04.575 --> 00:15:06.700
Don't say that. It's not true.

00:15:06.908 --> 00:15:10.450
Jules, tell me. Did you have
any idea about any of it?

00:15:10.658 --> 00:15:12.575
How would I have known?

00:15:12.783 --> 00:15:16.825
We have a deal. My domain's the kitchen
and the bedroom. His is the office.

00:15:17.033 --> 00:15:19.908
- I held up my end of the bargain.
- You poor thing.

00:15:20.117 --> 00:15:23.700
Believe me, if I'd known, I'd have
taken my girls out of the country.

00:15:23.908 --> 00:15:25.867
It's them I'm concerned about.

00:15:26.075 --> 00:15:28.742
Having to live with the shame
of what your father's done?

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.742
- Maybe we shouldn't talk about this.
- Oh, no, I don't mind.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.158
To be honest, I blame myself.

00:15:35.367 --> 00:15:38.742
I feel like I should have known,
like I should have sensed it somehow.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.617
- How could you? You had no idea.
- Don't beat yourself up. You're a victim.

00:15:42.825 --> 00:15:44.533
You're right, I know.
It's just...

00:15:44.742 --> 00:15:46.158
What else can I do?

00:15:46.367 --> 00:15:50.825
- I have the name of a great attorney.
- A good attorney could really help Jimmy.

00:15:51.033 --> 00:15:54.242
It's for Julie, to divorce his sorry ass.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:58.617
Girls, this isn't helping Julie relax.
Isn't that why we're here?

00:15:58.825 --> 00:16:02.242
Kirsten's right.
I mean, you wouldn't get a divorce.

00:16:04.075 --> 00:16:05.867
Would you?

00:16:11.742 --> 00:16:13.658
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:16:14.575 --> 00:16:19.033
How do you feel about
a little thing that I like to call...

00:16:19.575 --> 00:16:21.117
...the IMAX Experience?

00:16:22.033 --> 00:16:25.033
- This town sucks. The best I could do.
- I can't.

00:16:25.242 --> 00:16:27.033
I'm hanging out with Marissa tonight.

00:16:27.242 --> 00:16:29.575
We'll get a third ticket.
I doubt it'll sell out.

00:16:29.783 --> 00:16:31.575
Well, she's got her sister.

00:16:31.783 --> 00:16:33.783
Fine. Four tickets then. I like Kaitlin.

00:16:33.992 --> 00:16:36.283
She's nice, and she's smart,
for a fifth-grader.

00:16:36.492 --> 00:16:38.825
Actually, I...

00:16:39.033 --> 00:16:42.533
...was gonna go over there.
Help her babysit.

00:16:44.408 --> 00:16:45.700
Nice. The babysit.

00:16:45.908 --> 00:16:49.158
I see. Stepping it up, taking it
to the next level. I can respect that.

00:16:49.367 --> 00:16:51.158
Yeah. Hey, Donnie, I'm gonna head out.

00:16:51.367 --> 00:16:55.408
I'm gonna head out too. I can't believe
we survived this shift. I'm so hung-over.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.242
What are you gonna do now?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.492
- I got plans.
- All right, man.

00:17:02.533 --> 00:17:07.033
I have an extra ticket to the IMAX.
Shark movie, hammerheads, very violent.

00:17:07.242 --> 00:17:09.367
- What are you, like, 8?
- Got a better idea?

00:17:09.575 --> 00:17:13.658
I got a house party in Long Beach.
Six kegs, crazy honeys.

00:17:13.867 --> 00:17:16.200
- Okay, yes. That is better.
- Wanna come?

00:17:18.408 --> 00:17:19.575
Is that...? Is that cool?

00:17:20.075 --> 00:17:22.325
- Let me just change up.
- All right.

00:17:25.325 --> 00:17:28.617
- I do enjoy the crazy honeys.
- You're not going.

00:17:28.825 --> 00:17:30.825
Okay, Mom, except that I am.

00:17:31.033 --> 00:17:33.533
It's a shady neighborhood.
It's pretty hardcore.

00:17:33.742 --> 00:17:35.617
Dude, it's Long Beach, not Chechnya.

00:17:35.825 --> 00:17:38.075
Guys like Donnie,
you don't exactly know them...

00:17:38.283 --> 00:17:40.742
...and they don't exactly know
kids like you.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.533
- So I shouldn't talk about Grey Poupon?
- How you gonna get there?

00:17:43.742 --> 00:17:46.825
I got my mom's Range Rover.
Well, I'll park it up the street.

00:17:47.033 --> 00:17:49.950
Look, man, Donnie's a good guy, right?
He's cool, right?

00:17:50.158 --> 00:17:53.825
So maybe this way we can all
be friends. We can all hang out.

00:17:55.533 --> 00:17:57.325
- You boys game or what?
- Yeah, man.

00:17:59.283 --> 00:18:00.992
We'll go for one hour.

00:18:03.908 --> 00:18:07.075
Do you know how long it's been
since I've had a steak?

00:18:07.283 --> 00:18:08.700
I live with three vegetarians.

00:18:08.908 --> 00:18:11.700
You know how long it's been
since we had beer in the house?

00:18:11.908 --> 00:18:13.658
I'm so sick of chardonnay and merlot.

00:18:13.867 --> 00:18:15.117
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:18:17.992 --> 00:18:20.867
You wanna grab that?
These are almost done.

00:18:25.283 --> 00:18:28.325
- Hello?
- Jimmy? Did I dial your number?

00:18:28.533 --> 00:18:30.158
No, no. I'm at your place.

00:18:30.575 --> 00:18:31.992
Oh, working on the case?

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:34.742
Well, we're taking a break, actually.

00:18:35.367 --> 00:18:36.408
With Sandy?

00:18:36.617 --> 00:18:39.408
Yeah. We're doing guy stuff.

00:18:41.283 --> 00:18:44.867
All right. Well, when you finish
doing guy stuff...

00:18:45.075 --> 00:18:49.200
...would you have Sandy give me a call?
I called to see if everything was okay.

00:18:49.408 --> 00:18:52.325
- Is it?
- Well...

00:18:52.533 --> 00:18:54.200
I guess. I don't know.

00:18:54.408 --> 00:18:57.908
You know,
I've been really worried about you.

00:18:58.117 --> 00:19:00.492
Thanks. I appreciate it.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.700
Well, I'll talk to you when I get back.
Take care, Jimmy.

00:19:07.658 --> 00:19:10.408
Your concern for my husband
is really touching.

00:19:12.117 --> 00:19:15.158
Can you believe that? God.

00:19:43.117 --> 00:19:45.075
She really is a dancer.

00:19:54.408 --> 00:19:57.533
Chino. Come here, man.
I want you to meet some of my boys.

00:19:57.742 --> 00:20:00.617
- We have 45 minutes.
- We should invite her to the pool house.

00:20:00.825 --> 00:20:02.533
- Don't say "pool house."
- Right.

00:20:02.742 --> 00:20:06.158
Oh, dude, I thought you said
you played before.

00:20:06.408 --> 00:20:09.033
Well, some people
have a natural talent.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:11.867
Not me.

00:20:12.075 --> 00:20:15.742
I haven't played video games in, like...
I can't remember last time I played.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:17.992
Are we old? Because...

00:20:18.658 --> 00:20:22.575
...if I didn't know better,
I'd swear I was still 16.

00:20:22.783 --> 00:20:25.950
Hell, I'm still 22.
It was the best year of my life.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:30.700
- Yeah? Why 22?
- That's when I met Kirsten.

00:20:32.742 --> 00:20:36.283
- Why 16?
- Oh, that's when...

00:20:37.658 --> 00:20:39.617
...I met Kirsten.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:52.450
- Hello?
- Marissa?

00:20:52.658 --> 00:20:55.242
Hey. Where are you?

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:59.242
What'd I tell you, man?
How much better is this than Newport?

00:21:00.408 --> 00:21:03.450
I got dragged to a party,
but I'm leaving. I'm on my way.

00:21:03.658 --> 00:21:07.408
I just gotta get
Seth away from this...

00:21:07.617 --> 00:21:10.075
- This dancer.
- Dancer?

00:21:10.575 --> 00:21:14.575
It's a long story, but I'll be there soon.

00:21:14.783 --> 00:21:17.742
- Save me some mac and cheese?
- Sure. See you.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:24.033
- No, no way...
- Seth.

00:21:27.117 --> 00:21:28.700
One second.

00:21:28.908 --> 00:21:32.200
Hang on a second. Listen,
I am really connecting with this girl.

00:21:32.408 --> 00:21:36.367
She just moved here with her sister from
Uzbekistan, they're saving for a condo.

00:21:36.575 --> 00:21:38.033
Nice. That hits here.

00:21:38.242 --> 00:21:42.367
Now, she does have a serious boyfriend,
but she's looking into...

00:21:45.158 --> 00:21:47.075
Good luck with the condo.

00:21:50.408 --> 00:21:53.825
Some dude just demo'd
a Range Rover.

00:21:54.033 --> 00:21:56.408
That car's messed up.

00:22:09.367 --> 00:22:11.950
This happened in the parking lot
of the IMAX theater?

00:22:13.367 --> 00:22:15.075
Shark movies bring out
a rough crowd.

00:22:18.033 --> 00:22:21.908
I'll call the insurance company, but
you're explaining this to your mother.

00:22:22.075 --> 00:22:24.033
It could get ugly.

00:22:29.575 --> 00:22:30.950
Yeah.

00:22:33.575 --> 00:22:34.783
So did you call Marissa?

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:37.867
I tried her again this morning.
She doesn't wanna talk.

00:22:38.033 --> 00:22:41.950
- I'm sorry I salted your game, man.
- I gotta get to work.

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:53.408
I'll give you Richard's number
when we get back. He's the best.

00:22:53.575 --> 00:22:55.575
He did Carol's divorce.
She got everything.

00:22:55.742 --> 00:22:57.533
Thanks. That'd be great.

00:22:57.700 --> 00:23:01.033
- You're really considering a divorce?
- Why, are you gonna tell Jimmy?

00:23:01.408 --> 00:23:03.283
Julie needs to protect herself.

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:06.825
I can't believe you're encouraging this.
When your husband had an affair...

00:23:06.992 --> 00:23:09.242
...no one gave you
a divorce attorney's number.

00:23:09.408 --> 00:23:11.825
Kirsten, that was very uncalled-for.

00:23:11.992 --> 00:23:15.742
What's uncalled-for is your
$500-a-day coke habit in college.

00:23:15.908 --> 00:23:19.492
- It was just sophomore year.
- What Jimmy did was wrong.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:22.575
Spare me. You have a Guatemalan family
cleaning your house...

00:23:22.742 --> 00:23:24.992
...for less than minimum wage.

00:23:26.242 --> 00:23:31.075
I have spent this entire weekend
listening to you women judge Jimmy.

00:23:31.242 --> 00:23:34.992
Yes, he made a big mistake. But life is
complicated, and none of us is perfect.

00:23:35.158 --> 00:23:38.325
- Not even you, Julie.
- And what is that supposed to mean?

00:23:38.492 --> 00:23:41.450
He didn't buy ponies and jewelry
for himself.

00:23:41.617 --> 00:23:44.450
How interesting that you
should take his side.

00:23:44.617 --> 00:23:46.283
Shower time. Limo leaves at 6.

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:49.992
He did this to give you everything.
And now you're just gonna leave him?

00:23:50.158 --> 00:23:51.617
He lied to me, Kirsten.

00:23:51.783 --> 00:23:54.200
You lied to yourself! I know Jimmy.

00:23:54.367 --> 00:23:58.783
I know. I've heard. He still has
your prom photo up on our wall.

00:23:59.867 --> 00:24:01.617
- It's all in the past.
- Really?

00:24:01.783 --> 00:24:05.950
You think it's a coincidence that we
ended up living next door to you?

00:24:06.117 --> 00:24:10.158
I'm the one who married him.
This is my problem, not yours.

00:24:13.825 --> 00:24:15.700
Who knew that
when he knocked me up...

00:24:15.867 --> 00:24:19.575
...it'd be the best thing
that ever happened to you?

00:24:36.117 --> 00:24:37.742
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:24:37.908 --> 00:24:41.117
Your dad let me in.
Seems like he's doing better.

00:24:41.450 --> 00:24:43.033
Yeah, I guess.

00:24:44.742 --> 00:24:46.617
Do you need to get that?

00:24:46.783 --> 00:24:49.992
It's probably just Summer calling
about another party at Holly's.

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.492
Yes, another one of those.

00:24:53.658 --> 00:24:56.325
- So how'd it go with the dancer?
- Actually...

00:24:56.492 --> 00:25:00.367
...that's what I wanted to talk about.
Last night was totally my fault.

00:25:00.533 --> 00:25:04.700
Okay? Ryan was extremely bummed he
didn't get to make his Blockbuster night.

00:25:04.867 --> 00:25:08.242
I know you're going through a lot,
and you didn't need to get stood up.

00:25:08.450 --> 00:25:12.408
- So I apologize.
- Wow, that's very...

00:25:12.575 --> 00:25:15.533
...thoughtful.
- Well, he's pretty mad at me right now.

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:18.200
Why don't you help me out?
How about another date?

00:25:20.450 --> 00:25:22.867
He's a good cook.

00:25:30.242 --> 00:25:33.825
I tell you, one good swing...

00:25:33.992 --> 00:25:35.950
...and I love this game.

00:25:36.117 --> 00:25:37.575
Nice drive.

00:25:39.492 --> 00:25:43.242
So I talked to my friend,
the securities attorney, this morning.

00:25:43.408 --> 00:25:44.950
Working on the weekend?

00:25:45.117 --> 00:25:47.283
Working for you, to keep you out of jail.

00:25:47.450 --> 00:25:50.658
- He's pretty sure he can make it happen.
- Excellent.

00:25:50.825 --> 00:25:53.158
It's contingent upon you
making full restitution.

00:25:53.783 --> 00:25:57.950
You'll lose your license and never be
allowed near an investment account.

00:25:58.117 --> 00:26:01.992
- But little or no jail time.
- So I gotta pay back everything I lost.

00:26:02.742 --> 00:26:05.992
And even then, there are no guarantees.
But it's your only option.

00:26:06.158 --> 00:26:10.242
Well, that's not an option. I mean, where
the hell am I gonna find $4 million?

00:26:10.408 --> 00:26:14.325
Your house is valued at 3.2, you got
2.6 in equity. That's a good start.

00:26:14.492 --> 00:26:16.575
You want me to sell my house?

00:26:16.742 --> 00:26:18.325
Julie will...

00:26:18.492 --> 00:26:21.283
- She'll leave me.
- Julie cares about you and the kids.

00:26:21.450 --> 00:26:24.450
She won't care about losing the house,
if it means keeping you.

00:26:24.617 --> 00:26:26.158
Whose wife are we talking about?

00:26:27.908 --> 00:26:30.158
No. We gotta come up
with something else.

00:26:30.325 --> 00:26:33.325
This is it. This is a gift. Be grateful.

00:26:34.367 --> 00:26:36.658
- Grateful?
- Did you think it would just go away?

00:26:36.825 --> 00:26:38.992
That there would be no consequences?
Get real.

00:26:39.158 --> 00:26:42.658
Who are you to tell me to get real?
You live in a fantasy land.

00:26:42.825 --> 00:26:45.992
Your wife is rich. You live in
a house you've never paid for.

00:26:46.158 --> 00:26:48.450
You get fired,
Kirsten wouldn't even notice it.

00:26:48.617 --> 00:26:52.867
You have no idea what
it's like to provide for a family.

00:26:55.450 --> 00:27:00.492
I think there's more to providing
for a family than money.

00:27:00.783 --> 00:27:05.075
Wanna be there when Marissa graduates?
You wanna watch Kaitlin grow up?

00:27:05.242 --> 00:27:07.908
You can start over.
You can start a new life.

00:27:08.242 --> 00:27:11.367
I don't want a new life.
I want my old one back.

00:27:13.450 --> 00:27:15.992
But I guess
that's not gonna happen, huh?

00:27:19.075 --> 00:27:20.408
- Hey.
- What's up?

00:27:20.575 --> 00:27:23.492
Seth Cohen, your friendly
neighborhood pimp, at your service.

00:27:23.658 --> 00:27:26.075
I talked with Marissa.
It's totally handled.

00:27:26.242 --> 00:27:28.325
I'll be right back with your drinks.

00:27:28.492 --> 00:27:29.825
What are you talking about?

00:27:29.992 --> 00:27:33.908
It turns out that I'm skilled at getting
a date, provided it's not for me.

00:27:34.075 --> 00:27:38.367
You'll have the house to yourself. She'll
be coming over, and you'll be cooking.

00:27:38.533 --> 00:27:39.908
- What's up, man?
- Hey.

00:27:40.075 --> 00:27:42.825
What's the agenda for tonight?
Any plans?

00:27:42.992 --> 00:27:44.742
- Not really, no.
- Anything going on?

00:27:44.908 --> 00:27:47.658
There's a lame beach party,
typical Newport scene.

00:27:47.825 --> 00:27:50.242
You know what, man? We should go.

00:27:51.075 --> 00:27:56.033
No. It's not for me. It's gonna be
water-polo guys and their girlfriends.

00:27:56.200 --> 00:27:58.700
I don't get the whole
water-polo thing down here.

00:27:58.867 --> 00:28:01.117
Nor do I. A bunch of dudes
who enjoy wearing Speedos.

00:28:01.283 --> 00:28:04.533
- What do they know about partying?
- I couldn't agree more.

00:28:04.867 --> 00:28:06.367
But the girls are hot.

00:28:06.533 --> 00:28:10.283
So with the right attitude
and a couple cocktails, it could be fun.

00:28:10.450 --> 00:28:13.200
If it's not, we'll make it fun.
Life is what you make it.

00:28:13.908 --> 00:28:16.367
- That's very wise, Donnie.
- Tell you what, man.

00:28:16.533 --> 00:28:20.033
Here's what we'll do. We're gonna go.
I'll call a couple of my boys.

00:28:20.200 --> 00:28:23.533
We'll drink their beer, dance with
their honeys and have a good time.

00:28:23.700 --> 00:28:24.783
- All right.
- All right?

00:28:24.950 --> 00:28:26.408
All right.

00:28:30.825 --> 00:28:33.908
Enough with the moody scowl thing.
Please, it's not a big deal.

00:28:34.075 --> 00:28:37.700
- You're taking him to a Newport party?
- Exactly. It'll be on my turf.

00:28:37.867 --> 00:28:41.908
I don't have turf, but if I did, this would
be it. And Summer will be there.

00:28:42.075 --> 00:28:45.992
- I don't know about this, Seth.
- I do. It's fine. Not a big deal. I promise.

00:28:46.158 --> 00:28:49.158
Now, you got a date, okay?
So you have to go.

00:28:50.700 --> 00:28:52.658
Make me proud.

00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:56.325
Put a sock on the door.

00:29:19.408 --> 00:29:20.825
Hey.

00:29:22.950 --> 00:29:25.117
I brought you some leftovers.

00:29:26.117 --> 00:29:28.742
It should go well
with the grilled cheese.

00:29:29.117 --> 00:29:30.367
My specialty.

00:29:30.533 --> 00:29:34.242
- Very fancy.
- Hey, don't knock it till you've tried it.

00:29:38.367 --> 00:29:39.950
Dinner is served.

00:29:50.283 --> 00:29:51.908
Kind of lame, right?

00:29:52.075 --> 00:29:55.450
I'm seeing lots of potential
in here, actually.

00:30:09.242 --> 00:30:10.575
Hey.

00:30:14.950 --> 00:30:17.117
Where's Marissa?

00:30:17.658 --> 00:30:19.242
She's at home.

00:30:20.408 --> 00:30:21.742
We're...

00:30:21.908 --> 00:30:23.908
...sort of taking a break.

00:30:24.408 --> 00:30:26.325
You are?

00:30:31.408 --> 00:30:33.158
Are you okay?

00:30:46.200 --> 00:30:48.742
That was the best grilled cheese ever.

00:30:48.908 --> 00:30:51.200
Yeah. Your mac and cheese
was pretty good too.

00:30:51.367 --> 00:30:53.825
Yeah? Well, it tasted better last night.

00:30:57.117 --> 00:30:59.033
Hey.

00:31:03.617 --> 00:31:06.700
- But, hey, we're here now, right?
- Yeah.

00:31:07.117 --> 00:31:09.200
I'm glad we are.

00:31:13.367 --> 00:31:15.492
So how are you with everything?

00:31:15.658 --> 00:31:18.158
I'm okay, I guess.

00:31:18.325 --> 00:31:21.033
I mean, I still don't know
what's gonna happen.

00:31:21.283 --> 00:31:23.367
My parents are fighting all the time.

00:31:25.867 --> 00:31:27.867
My family's not perfect.

00:31:29.283 --> 00:31:31.783
Not even close, but...

00:31:33.575 --> 00:31:36.700
...I just don't want us to fall apart.

00:31:41.492 --> 00:31:44.367
Let's do something fun.
You can still have fun, right?

00:31:44.533 --> 00:31:46.158
I don't know.

00:31:48.700 --> 00:31:50.867
What if you don't have a choice?

00:31:51.033 --> 00:31:52.992
What does that mean?

00:31:54.950 --> 00:31:57.283
No, no, no. Don't. Stop.

00:31:59.117 --> 00:32:00.658
Okay.

00:32:07.325 --> 00:32:09.117
I'm taking you with me.

00:32:43.742 --> 00:32:47.117
What's up, girl?
You don't like to dance?

00:32:47.450 --> 00:32:49.575
Not with you.

00:32:51.283 --> 00:32:53.492
I'm trying to get to the bar.

00:32:53.867 --> 00:32:56.117
You're fine, you know that?

00:32:56.283 --> 00:32:57.867
Good one.

00:32:58.033 --> 00:33:00.992
But aren't you, like, the busboy?

00:33:02.408 --> 00:33:05.575
- Random.
- Who is that guy?

00:33:06.450 --> 00:33:08.575
What's up? Somebody got a problem?

00:33:08.950 --> 00:33:09.992
Hey, hey.

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:14.575
- What's going on?
- These kids are mad-dogging me.

00:33:14.950 --> 00:33:18.408
- Then why don't we go? I'm ready.
- No, I'm ready.

00:33:20.867 --> 00:33:25.575
Yeah, what? That's what I'm saying.
Life is what you make it.

00:33:32.700 --> 00:33:35.533
Hurry up, I'm freezing.

00:33:38.908 --> 00:33:42.575
- You've got goosebumps.
- I know. Towel.

00:33:42.742 --> 00:33:44.700
All right. Here.

00:33:48.450 --> 00:33:51.283
- You want a sweatshirt?
- No. Can I borrow a tank top...

00:33:51.450 --> 00:33:54.825
...so I can look as cool as you?
- Yeah. You wanna go back in the pool?

00:33:54.992 --> 00:33:56.367
No.

00:34:04.408 --> 00:34:06.242
Do you have to...?

00:34:08.617 --> 00:34:10.158
I'm sorry.

00:34:15.075 --> 00:34:18.492
- Hello?
- Hey, it's Seth. Donnie's kind of psycho.

00:34:20.492 --> 00:34:22.325
Okay, not really a good time
right now.

00:34:22.492 --> 00:34:26.325
I wouldn't call if it wasn't serious.
Take my dad's car, meet me at Holly's.

00:34:28.033 --> 00:34:29.867
I'll be right there.

00:34:32.325 --> 00:34:34.992
Okay. So that was Seth.

00:34:35.158 --> 00:34:36.242
I gotta go pick him up.

00:34:36.408 --> 00:34:39.742
- He's at Holly's if you want to...
- I can't go there.

00:34:39.908 --> 00:34:41.450
Right.

00:34:42.783 --> 00:34:44.783
Okay. So...

00:34:48.283 --> 00:34:50.283
Sorry. I...

00:34:50.450 --> 00:34:52.075
No. It's okay.

00:35:07.117 --> 00:35:09.033
You know how long
I've wanted to do this?

00:35:09.200 --> 00:35:11.158
As long as I have?

00:35:12.158 --> 00:35:14.700
You guys should have
broken up a long time ago.

00:35:21.867 --> 00:35:23.867
No. Chill. Chill!

00:35:24.033 --> 00:35:25.242
Seriously, relax.

00:35:25.408 --> 00:35:28.075
- What's up, bro? You want a drink?
- No, no.

00:35:28.242 --> 00:35:29.408
- You sure?
- Yes.

00:35:29.575 --> 00:35:31.325
It's vodka, very good. I'll do the...

00:35:34.658 --> 00:35:36.783
That sounded expensive.

00:35:37.533 --> 00:35:38.992
Come on.

00:35:40.950 --> 00:35:42.783
You go. I'II...

00:35:42.950 --> 00:35:44.867
I'm right behind you.

00:35:49.992 --> 00:35:54.325
- That's my blender!
- Check it out. It's Abercrombie.

00:35:55.200 --> 00:35:57.408
Or are you Fitch?

00:35:57.575 --> 00:36:00.367
- Jackass, what's your problem?
- You.

00:36:00.533 --> 00:36:03.242
- Luke, you really don't want to be...
- Shut up, Cohen.

00:36:03.408 --> 00:36:05.367
How'd you get in here anyway?

00:36:06.158 --> 00:36:09.408
Look, I don't know who you are.
You best be leaving.

00:36:09.575 --> 00:36:12.283
Or what? What you gonna do, man?

00:36:12.450 --> 00:36:14.575
What, you afraid I'm gonna
mess up your hair?

00:36:14.742 --> 00:36:16.700
- Donnie.
- What's up, Ryan?

00:36:16.867 --> 00:36:20.492
Should've figured he's a friend of yours.
Take him back to the trailer park.

00:36:20.658 --> 00:36:23.367
- We should go.
- What did you say to me?

00:36:23.533 --> 00:36:25.742
All right. Let's go.

00:36:27.450 --> 00:36:30.158
What's up now?
Who's the tough guy now?

00:36:32.283 --> 00:36:35.617
How much you hate this kid? The way
he talks to you like you're trash?

00:36:36.200 --> 00:36:39.408
- What about you, Seth?
- Yeah, he's definitely flawed.

00:36:39.575 --> 00:36:42.825
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
- Look at the role reversal now.

00:36:42.992 --> 00:36:45.450
- Who's the bitch?
- Look, you scared him. Put it down.

00:36:45.617 --> 00:36:50.450
I'm just trying to have a good time. I'm
trying to have fun. You boys having fun?

00:36:53.825 --> 00:36:56.658
What's the matter with you, man?
I was just messing around.

00:36:56.825 --> 00:36:59.242
- Oh, my God!
- We gotta go. Let's go.

00:37:00.117 --> 00:37:03.242
Oh, my God.
Call an ambulance, somebody!

00:37:03.408 --> 00:37:05.825
- You're gonna be okay.
- Call the cops, 911.

00:37:09.533 --> 00:37:13.992
I guess this is me.
Thanks for a relaxing weekend, ladies.

00:37:14.158 --> 00:37:16.742
I'm off to fire my cleaning lady.

00:37:17.450 --> 00:37:20.033
- Okay. See you at spinning.
- Bye, Taryn.

00:37:32.658 --> 00:37:34.867
Is it warm in here?

00:37:35.033 --> 00:37:37.367
Could you turn the air on, please?

00:37:38.200 --> 00:37:41.117
I'm sorry if I upset you.
It wasn't my place.

00:37:52.783 --> 00:37:56.283
I remember as a kid,
if I saw a limousine driving...

00:37:56.450 --> 00:37:59.117
...I'd always try to see
through the tinted window...

00:37:59.283 --> 00:38:02.617
...wondering what kind of life
the people inside lived.

00:38:02.783 --> 00:38:06.950
How glamorous and lucky.
Who knew, right?

00:38:07.908 --> 00:38:09.408
You knew.

00:38:10.950 --> 00:38:14.033
You were probably in there,
staring back at me.

00:38:14.200 --> 00:38:16.658
Which means I've been
jealous of you since I was 8.

00:38:19.908 --> 00:38:23.408
When I met Jimmy, I had nothing.
No money.

00:38:25.075 --> 00:38:27.200
I don't wanna go back
to being nothing again.

00:38:27.867 --> 00:38:29.450
You won't.

00:38:29.617 --> 00:38:32.700
You have a family, you have Jimmy.
He loves you.

00:38:35.075 --> 00:38:36.575
Not as much as he loved you.

00:38:38.825 --> 00:38:40.408
But I knew that when I married him.

00:38:43.492 --> 00:38:47.450
I was winning the lottery.
Great guy, great life.

00:38:49.450 --> 00:38:52.033
And he was doing the honorable thing.

00:38:56.367 --> 00:38:58.158
It's your turn, Julie.

00:39:00.950 --> 00:39:02.408
Don't abandon him.

00:39:08.450 --> 00:39:10.367
Hey. It's me.

00:39:10.533 --> 00:39:12.533
Yeah. No.

00:39:13.367 --> 00:39:15.033
I'm sorry.

00:39:15.200 --> 00:39:16.992
I'm at the hospital.

00:39:17.158 --> 00:39:20.200
No. Everything's fine, but...

00:39:20.992 --> 00:39:22.908
...I think you'll wanna get down here.

00:39:26.158 --> 00:39:27.575
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:39:27.742 --> 00:39:29.700
Hi. How'd it go?

00:39:29.867 --> 00:39:31.617
Not well.

00:39:31.825 --> 00:39:33.200
How about you?

00:39:33.367 --> 00:39:34.908
The same.

00:39:35.533 --> 00:39:37.742
Sandy, what happened to our car?

00:39:39.158 --> 00:39:40.825
Seth will explain everything.

00:39:40.992 --> 00:39:43.533
- Where is he?
- I don't know. He's out, I guess.

00:39:49.617 --> 00:39:51.908
You bought beer?

00:39:54.283 --> 00:39:55.658
I miss beer.

00:40:02.492 --> 00:40:05.075
- Want a sip?
- I want more than that.

00:40:05.242 --> 00:40:06.658
Really?

00:40:07.700 --> 00:40:10.492
You know, the boys might be out
for a while.

00:40:18.117 --> 00:40:19.325
Hey.

00:40:20.575 --> 00:40:21.825
I didn't hear you come in.

00:40:24.742 --> 00:40:27.408
So how was your weekend?
You win the lottery?

00:40:28.575 --> 00:40:30.367
That's funny.

00:40:32.783 --> 00:40:36.408
Do you wanna sit or stand?
Because I've got some news.

00:40:38.367 --> 00:40:40.325
It's not gonna be easy.

00:40:40.492 --> 00:40:42.492
We've... Well...

00:40:42.658 --> 00:40:44.992
...you've got a decision to make.

00:40:46.492 --> 00:40:47.742
What is it, Jimmy?

00:40:48.742 --> 00:40:53.825
We can liquidate our assets,
sell the house...

00:40:55.367 --> 00:40:59.158
...and start all over with nothing
as a family.

00:41:00.158 --> 00:41:03.867
Or we can declare bankruptcy...

00:41:04.033 --> 00:41:05.908
...keep the house...

00:41:06.075 --> 00:41:09.950
...and I see you and the girls
in about eight to 10 years.

00:41:10.992 --> 00:41:15.408
It's up to you.
Whatever you wanna do, I'll do.

00:41:17.492 --> 00:41:21.325
The cops said Donnie wasn't gonna
get far before they caught him.

00:41:22.575 --> 00:41:26.742
If you wanna make some extra money,
I'm sure there's a job at the restaurant.

00:41:26.908 --> 00:41:32.283
No. That's okay. It'd be good to take
some "me" time, work on the novel.

00:41:33.242 --> 00:41:35.492
Tonight would make a good chapter.

00:41:38.117 --> 00:41:39.950
Are you scared?

00:41:42.992 --> 00:41:44.658
Yeah.

00:41:49.200 --> 00:41:51.533
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:54.783
He's okay.
He's with his parents, third floor.

00:41:54.950 --> 00:41:56.783
It's just his arm.

00:41:59.700 --> 00:42:02.533
So this guy, was he a friend of yours?

00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:04.658
No, not really.

00:42:07.367 --> 00:42:10.533
- Well, thanks for calling me.
- Yeah.

00:42:11.700 --> 00:42:13.117
I...

00:42:15.117 --> 00:42:18.367
- I should go.
- I can wait.

00:42:19.950 --> 00:42:22.825
No, it's okay. I might be a while.

00:42:38.783 --> 00:42:41.408
Never thought the day would end here.

00:42:42.033 --> 00:42:43.658
I'm sorry, man.

00:42:45.992 --> 00:42:48.992
You were right. I shouldn't have
brought Donnie to that party.

00:42:49.158 --> 00:42:53.158
No, it's my fault. If it wasn't for me,
you never would have met him.

00:42:53.325 --> 00:42:55.575
Luke wouldn't be in the hospital.

00:42:55.742 --> 00:42:59.950
I feel like ever since I got here,
everyone's life's just gotten worse.

00:43:00.158 --> 00:43:02.075
Not everyone.

00:43:03.700 --> 00:43:06.950
All I was thinking about
in that ambulance was...

00:43:07.117 --> 00:43:11.075
...I'm so gone, back to Chino.
Or worse.

00:43:11.242 --> 00:43:14.242
You're not going anywhere,
so don't worry about it.

00:43:15.075 --> 00:43:17.867
I do think from now on, though,
we gotta stick together...

00:43:18.033 --> 00:43:22.117
...because united we're unstoppable,
but divided it's like...

00:43:22.283 --> 00:43:25.075
- People get shot.
- That's what I'm saying.

00:43:25.242 --> 00:43:27.242
That's what I'm saying.
